WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.258
The CIS Controls cover a wide range of security topics including asset management, access control, vulnerability management, logging, monitoring, incident response, security awareness, and data protection.

2
00:00:14.258 --> 00:00:19.237
Together, these areas help organizations establish a balanced security program.

3
00:00:19.237 --> 00:00:24.146
A program that only focuses on one area may leave important gaps elsewhere.

4
00:00:24.146 --> 00:00:28.536
For example, asset inventory helps teams know what they need to protect.

5
00:00:28.536 --> 00:00:31.220
Access control limits who can use systems.

6
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:34.433
Vulnerability management helps reduce known weaknesses.

7
00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:37.227
Logging and monitoring help detect problems.

8
00:00:37.227 --> 00:00:44.461
Control families make the broader program easier to understand because they connect individual safeguards to security outcomes.
